<article class="env-lemma" id="0482">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0482">Lemma <span data-tag="0482">76.3.2</span>.</a> A radicial morphism of algebraic spaces is universally injective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a radicial morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. It is clear from the definition that given a morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(K) \to Y$ there is at most one lift of this morphism to a morphism into $X$. Hence we conclude that $f$ is universally injective by Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/040X" data-tag="040X">67.19.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>